2026-11-14T17:14:51+00:00 [29/221] basal cell carcinoma -> UNREADABLE: 'This looks like alopecia neoplastica, i.e. a cutaneous metastasis from the breast carcinoma. Among the listed options, the closest category is basal cell carcinoma, which can appear as a whitish, indurated plaque with arborizing vessels. The lesion could also be a morpheaform or sclerosing BCC, which fits the hard whitish plaque with arborizing vessels and loss of follicular openings. A metastasis would be the more likely real answer, but it is not on the list, so I am choosing from the options given.\n\nbasal cell carcinoma'
