2026-11-14T17:18:02+00:00 [77/221] pigmented benign keratosis -> UNREADABLE: 'This sounds like giant pigmented genital lesions, probably pigmented giant condyloma or a giant seborrheic keratosis. The description of brownish-black greasy, lobulated nodules over the genitals and groin with a 10-year course is most consistent with a pigmented benign keratosis (extensive genital seborrheic keratosis or pigmented verrucous lesions). Of the options, pigmented benign keratosis is the best fit.\n\npigmented benign keratosis'
