2026-11-14T17:20:31+00:00 [114/221] nevus -> UNREADABLE: 'This is a young woman with a 5-month-old reddish-brown dome-shaped hyperkeratotic nodule on the lower leg. The dermoscopy shows ring-like whitish scale, glomerular and dotted vessels, milia-like cysts and light brown globules. Together these point to a Spitz-type melanocytic lesion, though the hyperkeratosis, scale and milia-like cysts could also fit a keratinizing lesion.\n\nBecause it is pigmented, symmetrical and well demarcated, and because dotted and glomerular vessels with globules are typical of Spitz nevus, nevus is the most likely diagnosis. Hyperkeratotic Spitz nevi with ring-like scale have been described, so this fits.\n\nnevus'
