2026-11-14T17:24:02+00:00 [167/221] squamous cell carcinoma -> UNREADABLE: 'This picture is chromoblastomycosis (verrucous plaques, sclerotic bodies, a farmer in Brazil), which is not among the options. Of the listed choices, squamous cell carcinoma is the closest, since chronic verrucous lesions of this kind can mimic it or undergo malignant transformation.\n\nsquamous cell carcinoma'
2026-11-14T17:24:07+00:00 [168/221] actinic keratosis -> UNREADABLE: 'This is a cutaneous horn on the finger of a farmer. Cutaneous horns arise from underlying lesions such as actinic keratosis or squamous cell carcinoma. A 2 cm horn with a broad base on the palmar finger is more concerning for an underlying squamous cell carcinoma (the palmar location is sun-protected, and a broad base suggests malignancy). Published case reports of a palmar cutaneous horn describe squamous cell carcinoma at its base.\n\nsquamous cell carcinoma'
